An alternative view....

On Mar 8, 7:17 pm, "sjdevn...@yahoo.com" <sjdevn...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> > While looking over the spoiler it says to wish for a blessed wand of
> > polymorph.  And I'm wondering why a blessed
> > wand?  Is there a difference?
>
> Not really unless it gets cursed, but may as well wish it blessed.

The key point here not explained is that you lose nothing for
specifying "blessed" in the wish, it won't mess you up in any way to
ask for it, so why not get it?  Other than that, the 1% chance of a
wand exploding is laughable unless you REALLY want to make sure you
don't waste the wand (like with a wand of wishing).


> > It also says wish for an uncursed magic marker.  Why not blessed? (I'm
> > thinking so you can write cursed scrolls...)
>
> Bless a stack of 15+ paper, the marker will write blessed on them and
> cursed on cursed scrolls.

I usually get a blessed marker because most scrolls are better blessed
then cursed.  Making use of cursed scrolls is a relatively advanced
tactic (for reverse genocide, for disenchanting objects to make
reaching max safe enchantment easier, for level teleport, etc).  The
problem with blessing the scrolls instead of the marker is that it's
more wasteful of holy water.  Maximum holy water supply is limited to
potion supply, and if you're not farming to get lots of potions it is
worth conserving.

> > So what should I wish for? I have 3 after recharging. (It came with just 1)
> > (what do I need to ascend - in about 10 years I've only ascended 3 Valks
> > and 2 rangers.)
