> No reflection?  Ugh.  If you can find silver scales somewhere and a
> COMR, do that.  If not, if you can find an "oR do that.

But do not abandon magic resistance in favor of reflection!  One
doesn't need reflection to win, and I've done without it several
times, but without magic resistance you can be killed in one turn by
the next Wizard of Yendor to stroll down the hall, or failing that by
Death himself.

The true advantages of reflection to a late-game character, to my eye,
are:
- Protects items from ray destruction.  It's possible to lose many
rings and wands on Air without it (as happened to me on my first
ascension).
- As far as dying goes, while breath attacks from most dragons become
almost harmless as you gain hit points and resistances, black dragons
are a special problem.  The only sure ways to survive that are to have
disintegration-resistance (preferably from eating a black dragon, but
also possible from black dragon scales or BDSM) or reflection.  And,
if you just resist, then you can lose equipment to disintegration
rays.


> Personally I'd ditch the GoP for GoDex or leather and outfit myself
> with "oR and a robe.

Depends on what his no-GoP strength is.  If it's not 18/** then it
could put him into Burdened, which is bad news.  In any case, don't
take off that GDSM unless you have something to make up for it, like a
cloak of magic resistance.


> I'd be on the lookout for jumping boots, too, or at least speed until
> you can find jumping.

Speed is more universally helpful (more attacks and chances to get out
of instant peril), while jumping is more useful to experienced
ascenders.


> > Rings of Poly Control and Slow Digest
> > also poly/conflict/ invisibility
>
> Conflict, levitation, free action, and telecontrol are the big 4 (the
> latter only until you get it intrinsically).

Getting teleport control safely is never assured, it's usually done by
eating tengus, who can also confer teleportitus.  Polymorph can be
dangerous late in the game since it can destroy your armor.  Slow
digestion gets less useful as the food rations pile up.  Free Action
and Conflict, however, cannot be easily attained in any other way, and
conflict, used well, is one of the most potent sources of aid you can
find.


